Qoder check-in follows the official desktop campaign API. CN and Global use the
same paths on different hosts:

  GET  https://openapi.qoder.com.cn/sash/api/v1/me/campaigns
  POST https://openapi.qoder.com.cn/sash/api/v1/me/campaigns/{campaignId}/claim
  GET  https://openapi.qoder.sh/sash/api/v1/me/campaigns
  POST https://openapi.qoder.sh/sash/api/v1/me/campaigns/{campaignId}/claim

CN was observed from Qoder CN 0.3.4. Global was observed from the Qoder desktop
client on 2026-10-07. The worker reuses the pinned AuthManager and does not copy
Qoder's campaign UI.

Known limitation (verified 2026-10-17): the paths are the same, but the two
regions do NOT expose the daily check-in identically to the worker. CN's campaign
service returns a claimable CLAIM_BENEFIT campaign to the worker's tokens, so
auto check-in works for CN. Global's campaign service (openapi.qoder.sh) returns
only a BOGO subscription promo (VIEW_DETAILS) to the worker's tokens and reserves
the claimable daily check-in for the Qoder desktop client's own session token
(observed `dt-sp…`-prefixed, ~34 chars). The worker's loginWithPAT yields a
`jt-…`-prefixed token (~27 chars) and loginWithDeviceFlow yields a `dt-…`-prefixed
token (~27 chars); neither has the scope to see/claim the Global daily check-in.
Global accounts therefore cannot be auto-checked-in by the worker; leave their
auto_checkin off and rely on the desktop client.
